			<h1 class=3D"entry-title">3 Ways to Disable IPv6 in Windows 10 / 8 / 7</=
h1>
			<small class=3D"meta">
  			<span class=3D"alignleft">
          <span class=3D"updated">August 20, 2020</span> updated by <span c=
lass=3D"vcard author"><span class=3D"fn"><a href=3D"https://plus.google.com=
/106896562588555672604">Admin</a></span></span>
            			</span>
        <a href=3D"https://www.top-password.com/blog/disable-ipv6-in-window=
s/#comments" class=3D"alignright button-style" rel=3D"nofollow">Leave a rep=
ly =C2=BB</a>
      </small>

			<div class=3D"entry">
				<div class=3D"at-above-post addthis_tool" data-url=3D"https://www.top-p=
assword.com/blog/disable-ipv6-in-windows/"></div><p>IPv6 causes connectivit=
y issues? IPv6 is the latest version of the Internet Protocol, which is sup=
posed to replace IPv4. However, most websites or softwares don=E2=80=99t wo=
rk with IPv6 yet. It is common for IT administrators to disable IPv6 to fix=
 some unknown, networking-related issue. In this tutorial we=E2=80=99ll sho=
w you 3 easy methods to disable IPv6 in Windows 10 / 8 / 7.</p>
<p><strong>Method 1: Disable IPv6 in Network Adapter Properties</strong></p=
>
<ol>
<li>Press the Windows logo key + R to open the Run dialog. Type <strong>ncp=
a.cpl</strong> and hit Enter.
<p><img decoding=3D"async" src=3D"https://www.top-password.com/blog/wp-cont=
ent/uploads/2020/08/run-ncpa-command.png" alt=3D"" width=3D"401" height=3D"=
207" class=3D"alignnone size-full wp-image-16277">
</p></li>
<li>It will <a href=3D"https://www.top-password.com/blog/open-network-conne=
ctions-in-windows-10/" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer">open t=
he Network Connections window</a>. Right-click the network adapter you want=
 to disable IPv6 on, and then select <strong>Properties</strong>.
<p><img decoding=3D"async" loading=3D"lazy" src=3D"https://www.top-password=
.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/network-adapter-properties.png" alt=3D=
"" width=3D"586" height=3D"358" class=3D"alignnone size-full wp-image-16278=
">
</p></li>
<li>In order to disable IPv6, uncheck the box next to <strong>Internet Prot=
ocol Version 6 (TCP/IPv6)</strong>. Click <strong>OK</strong>.
<p><img decoding=3D"async" loading=3D"lazy" src=3D"https://www.top-password=
.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/uncheck-internet-protocol-version-6.pn=
g" alt=3D"" width=3D"365" height=3D"469" class=3D"alignnone size-full wp-im=
age-16279">
</p></li>
<li>You can use the same method to disable IPv6 for other network adapters.=
</li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Method 2: Disable IPv6 Using PowerShell</strong></p>
<ol>
<li>First, you need to <a href=3D"https://www.top-password.com/blog/5-ways-=
to-run-powershell-as-administrator-in-windows-10/" rel=3D"noopener noreferr=
er" target=3D"_blank">open Windows PowerShell as administrator</a>. Next, r=
un the following command to check the status of IPv6 for all network adapte=
rs available in your computer.
<p><code>Get-NetAdapterBinding -ComponentID ms_tcpip6</code></p>
<p><img decoding=3D"async" loading=3D"lazy" src=3D"https://www.top-password=
.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/check-network-adapters-ipv6.png" alt=
=3D"" width=3D"600" height=3D"249" class=3D"alignnone size-full wp-image-16=
280"></p>
<p> 	In my example, =E2=80=9C<em>Wi-Fi</em>=E2=80=9D is the name of the net=
work adapter I want to disable IPv6 on.</p></li>
<li>To disable IPv6 on a specific network adapter only, type the following =
command. Replace =E2=80=9C<em>Wi-Fi</em>=E2=80=9D with the name of your net=
work adapter card.<br>
<code>Disable-NetAdapterBinding -Name "Wi-Fi" -ComponentID ms_tcpip6</code>=
<p></p>
<p><img decoding=3D"async" loading=3D"lazy" src=3D"https://www.top-password=
.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/enable-ipv6-with-powershell.png" alt=
=3D"" width=3D"518" height=3D"124" class=3D"alignnone size-full wp-image-16=
281"></p>
<p>You can use the wildcard * to disable IPv6 on all network adapters, inst=
ead of disabling them one by one.<br>
<code>Disable-NetAdapterBinding -Name "*" -ComponentID ms_tcpip6</code></p>=
</li>
<li>Whenever you need to enable IPv6 again, just run this command:<br>
<code>Enable-NetAdapterBinding -name * -ComponentID ms_tcpip6</code></li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Method 3: Disable IPv6 Using Command Prompt</strong></p>
<ol>
<li><a href=3D"https://www.top-password.com/blog/open-elevated-command-prom=
pt-from-standard-user-in-windows/" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" target=3D"_b=
lank">Open the Command Prompt as administrator</a>, and execute this comman=
d to disable IPv6 completely:<br>
<code>reg add "HKLM\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Services\Tcpip6\Parameters" /v=
 DisabledComponents /t REG_DWORD /d 255 /f</code><p></p>
<p><img decoding=3D"async" loading=3D"lazy" src=3D"https://www.top-password=
.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/disable-ipv6-with-cmd.png" alt=3D"" wi=
dth=3D"584" height=3D"198" class=3D"alignnone size-full wp-image-16282">
</p></li>
<li>Restart the computer for changes to take effect. To verify if IPv6 is d=
isabled, run <code>ipconfig /all</code> and see if the interface shows IPv6=
 address.
<p><img decoding=3D"async" loading=3D"lazy" src=3D"https://www.top-password=
.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/ipconfig.png" alt=3D"" width=3D"597" h=
eight=3D"333" class=3D"alignnone size-full wp-image-16283"></p>
<p> 	To revert and enable IPv6, you can delete <strong>DisabledComponents</=
strong> registry key with this command:<br>
<code>reg delete "HKLM\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Services\Tcpip6\Parameters"=
 /v DisabledComponents /f</code></p></li>
</ol>
<p>That=E2=80=99s all there is to it.</p>
